  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_031, acc 0.678) uses scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted in a multimodal multiprofile setup. All other dimensions (RNA encoder, profile setting, aggregation, fusion) have been validated and show clear winners. The image encoder quality is the only major untested axis in the proven-best configuration. Image-only resnet50 was weak (0.208), yet in multimodal context it contributed ~4% over RNA-only, suggesting the image signal is underutilized. Question tested: Does upgrading the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l (a substantially stronger, pretrained vision transformer) increase the image modality's contribution and push overall accuracy beyond 0.678? Why best next: It is a single-variable, direct extension of the current best configuration, preserving all proven design choices while probing the largest remaining source of potential improvement. If ViT-L helps, it opens a new performance ceiling; if it does not, we learn the image modality's contribution is bounded by task relevance rather than encoder capacity, redirecting effort to RNA-side improvements (e.g., scgpt). This maximizes information gain per experiment under the limited budget."
}

